# The atlas

Import WebGraph from "../src/web_graph.lg".
Import TextSet from "../src/text_set.lg".
Import WebFormat from "../src/web_format.lg".
Import UiSite from "../src/ui_site.lg".
Import UiStage from "../src/ui_stage.lg".
Import UiAtlasRow from "../src/ui_atlas_row.lg".

The front page of macsad.com: every problem the factory holds, as a tree of
cohorts, collections and categories, each branch coloured by where its problems
stand. Only the cohorts load with the page; a branch's children are fetched when
it is opened, two hundred at a time, best ranked first.

## Page /

Head:
    <title>MaCSad — the atlas of open problems</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Every open problem the MaCSad factory works on, by stage, with kernel-checked results.">

State:
    Let rows be a new Seq of GraphNode.
    Let open be a new Seq of Text.
    Let waiting be "".
    Let error be "".
    Let problems always be sumTotals(rows).
    Let solved always be sumSolved(rows).

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/v1/graph/children?node=root" as Seq of GraphNode, then arrived.

    To arrived (answer: Result of Seq of GraphNode and HttpError):
        Set waiting to "".
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (kids):
                If length of kids is greater than 0:
                    Set rows to withChildren(rows, parentOrRoot(item 1 of kids), kids).
                Set error to "".
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.

    To toggle (id: Text):
        If holdsText(open, id):
            Set rows to withoutBelow(rows, id).
            Remove every o from open where o is equal to id.
        Otherwise:
            Push id to open.
            Set waiting to id.
            Get "/api/v1/graph/children?node=" + urlEncode(id) + "&limit=200" as Seq of GraphNode, then arrived.

    To more (id: Text):
        Set waiting to id.
        Get "/api/v1/graph/children?node=" + urlEncode(id) + "&limit=200&offset={shownChildren(rows, id)}" as Seq of GraphNode, then arrived.

View:
    {extends Site}
    {block content:}
      <section class="page-head">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">The atlas</div>
          <h1>Open problems, and how far the factory has got with each</h1>
          <p class="lede">Problems come from the OPDP difficulty atlas, the formalization lab and formal-conjectures.
            Each is ranked, given a formal LOGOS statement, attacked by contributors' models, and settled only by the kernel.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="totals">
          <div class="total"><b id="total-problems">{formatCount(problems)}</b><span>problems</span></div>
          <div class="total"><b id="total-solved">{formatCount(solved)}</b><span>solved</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="card">
        <StageLegend/>
      </div>
      {if error is not equal to "":}<p class="error-banner" role="alert" id="error">{error}</p>{end}
      <ul class="tree card" id="tree">
        {for each n in rows, keyed by n's id:}
          <AtlasRow n={n} open={holdsText(open, n's id)} waiting={waiting is equal to n's id} unfetched={unfetchedChildren(rows, n)} toggle={toggle} more={more}/>
        {else:}
          <li class="empty">Loading the atlas…</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
    {end}

## Test: the atlas opens on the cohorts with their totals

Given that GET "/api/v1/graph/children?node=root" answers 200 with """[{{"id": "cohort:A", "parentId": "", "problemId": "", "kind": "cohort", "label": "Atlas A", "stage": "ranked",
  "rankBp": 9, "depth": 1, "childCount": 2, "total": 1200, "ranked": 1197, "formalizing": 0, "formalized": 0,
  "inProgress": 0, "partial": 0, "solved": 3, "refuted": 0, "invalid": 0}}]""".
Expect that the count of ".tree-row" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#total-problems" is equal to "1,200".
Expect that the text of "#total-solved" is equal to "3".
Expect that the count of ".seg" is equal to 2.

## Test: opening a branch fetches its children and closing it hides them

Given that GET "/api/v1/graph/children?node=root" answers 200 with """[{{"id": "cohort:A", "parentId": "", "problemId": "", "kind": "cohort", "label": "A", "stage": "ranked",
  "rankBp": 9, "depth": 1, "childCount": 3, "total": 3, "ranked": 2, "formalizing": 0, "formalized": 0,
  "inProgress": 0, "partial": 0, "solved": 1, "refuted": 0, "invalid": 0}}]""".
Given that GET "/api/v1/graph/children?node=cohort%3AA&limit=200" answers 200 with """[{{"id": "problem:p1", "parentId": "cohort:A", "problemId": "p1", "kind": "problem", "label": "First", "stage": "solved",
  "rankBp": 5, "depth": 2, "childCount": 0, "total": 1, "ranked": 0, "formalizing": 0, "formalized": 0,
  "inProgress": 0, "partial": 0, "solved": 1, "refuted": 0, "invalid": 0}}]""".
Click ".caret".
Expect that the count of ".tree-row" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of ".tree-row a.label" is equal to "First".
Expect that the text of ".tree-more" is equal to "show 2 more".
Click ".caret".
Expect that the count of ".tree-row" is equal to 1.

## Test: an atlas the coordinator cannot serve says why

Given that GET "/api/v1/graph/children?node=root" answers 503 with "the database did not answer".
Expect that the text of "#error" is equal to "503: the database did not answer".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Loading the atlas…".
